  "prefLabel": "We 101.16 Drive shoe",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 101.16 “Drive shoe” means a hardened steel cylinder designed to be welded or threaded onto the end of the steel well casing and manufactured to provide a seal to the bedrock surface.\n\nSource. #6448, eff 1-29-97; ss by #7306, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9177, eff 6-13-08 (from We 101.13); renumbered by #12075 (formerly We 101.14)",
